# Layout break fix (2026-11-04, after first browser review)

Reported: promo bar not full width and clipped, main area showing only a
dark navy block, no sections visible below the header.

**Not a mount problem.** SSR already emitted every section in the right
order. Four Hydrogen-scaffold base rules were colliding with the full-bleed
PDP tree.

| Scaffold rule | Where | Effect |
|---|---|---|
| `aside { position:fixed; height:100vh; width:min(400px,100vw); right:-400px; box-shadow:... }` | `app/styles/app.css:87` | **The cause of the navy block.** `PromoBar` rendered as `<aside>`, so it inherited the off-canvas-drawer geometry: a 400px × 100vh navy column pushed 400px right, with a drop shadow. Its own `.bar` class only overrode `position`, `background` and `color` — not the size or offset. |
| `body > main { margin: 0 1rem 1rem 1rem }` | `app/styles/reset.css:81` | Every section inset 1rem; nothing could reach the viewport edge. |
| `section { padding: 1rem 0 → 2rem 0 }` | `app/styles/reset.css:85` | 2rem on every `<section>`; white gaps, and the pinned sections' `height: calc(100svh + travel)` no longer matched the sticky child's travel. |
| `li { margin-bottom: .5rem }` · `img { border-radius: 4px }` | `reset.css:126` · `app.css:11` | Gallery slides/thumbs, USP/spec/footer lists. |

## Changes

1. **`PromoBar/index.jsx`** — `<aside>` → `<div role="note" aria-label="Aktion">`.
   A promo banner is not a complementary landmark, and the bare `aside`
   element selector is spoken for by the scaffold.
2. **`app/styles/pdp-base.css`** (new) — linked from `root.jsx` *after*
   `reset.css` and `app.css`, so it wins the element-level ties:
   - `body > main:has(> .home) { margin: 0 }` — (0,1,2) beats `body > main`
     (0,0,2); scoped with `:has()` so other scaffold routes keep their gutter.
   - `:where(.home) section|li|img|h1–h4|p|a { … }` — `:where()` contributes
     0, so each rule stays at plain element specificity (0,0,1). It ties
     with the scaffold rule it cancels and **loses to every CSS Module
     class** (0,1,0), so no section's intentional spacing can be clobbered.
   - `html/body:has(… .home) { overflow-x: clip }` — the prototype's own
     guard (`prototype/css/site.css:2`). The pinned stages are laid out
     1920px wide and scaled by transform, so their layout width stays 1920.
     `clip`, not `hidden`, because `clip` does not create a scroll container
     and `position: sticky` keeps working.
   - `.overlay { z-index: 200 }` — the scaffold's cart/search/menu drawers
     are `z-index: 10` (`app.css:168`), below this page's sticky chrome.
     Without this an open drawer sat *under* the sub-nav and buy bar.
3. **Explicit `padding: 0`** on the four pinned `.section` rules
   (`StreadPro3D`, `KeyFeatures`, `SportstechLive`, `VideoShowcase`) and
   `padding: 0 0 96px` on `ProductGalleryBuybox` — so the scrub-travel box
   model never depends on stylesheet load order.
4. **Local list/image resets** where the scaffold defaults leaked into
   elements the modules had not sized: `.slide`, `.slide img`, `.usp`,
   `Reviews .bar`, `TechnicalData .spec`, `Footer .columnList li`.
5. **`StickyBuyBar` z-index 50 → 100** (as specified; still below the
   raised `.overlay`).

