# White-screen fix (2026-11-04)

## Diagnosis

The three things the report suspected were all fine:

| Check | Result |
|---|---|
| `body.html` empty? | No — 97,876 bytes, and in sync with the current `prototype/index.html` (promo copy matches: "KOSTENLOSER VERSAND · 30 TAGE TESTEN · 2 JAHRE GARANTIE") |
| `PrototypePage` rendered? | Yes — `($locale)._index.jsx:67` `return <PrototypePage />;` |
| `public/js` `img` `fig` present? | Yes — 18 / 23 / 44 files |
| Server response | HTTP 200, 125 KB |

The actual cause is that **on desktop the prototype page is empty until its
JS runs**. `prototype/css/site.css:13` hides `.mob`, and every desktop host
is a bare shell — `<section class="desk dstat" id="top" data-sec="dtop">
<div class="pinbox"></div></section>`. All desktop content is produced at
runtime by `buildStage`/`mountPinned`. So "white screen" meant the script
chain never finished.

**It never finished because of a StrictMode interaction in my own effect.**
`app/entry.client.jsx:13` wraps the app in `<StrictMode>`, which runs an
effect, tears it down, then runs it again. The effect held a `cancelled`
flag set by its cleanup:

```
run 1   -> booted = true, chain starts with cancelled = false
cleanup -> cancelled = true
run 2   -> booted is already true, returns immediately
chain   -> every remaining .then() sees cancelled and short-circuits
```

Net effect: only `/js/gsap.min.js` ever loaded. `sections.js`, `engine.js`
and `app.js` never ran, so nothing was ever built into the `.pinbox` hosts.

## Fix

`app/sections/PrototypePage/index.jsx` — removed the cancellation flag.
Booting the prototype is a one-shot global side effect on the document,
not component-scoped work, so there is nothing to cancel on unmount. The
`booted` module flag still guarantees a single boot, and `loadScript` is
independently idempotent via its `data-proto` attribute, so an HMR module
re-evaluation cannot double-load either.

## Hydrogen compatibility checklist

| # | Item | Status |
|---|------|--------|
| 7 | imports use `react-router` | ✓ 0 occurrences of `react-router-dom` in `app/` |
| 8 | no `window`/`document` during SSR | ✓ the only three references are inside `loadScript`, called only from `useEffect`; no module-scope DOM access |
| 9 | `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` client-only | **Kept server-rendered, deliberately** — see below |
| 10 | `suppressHydrationWarning` on the wrapper | ✓ added |
| 11 | scripts load after hydration | ✓ `useEffect`, client-only by definition |
| 12 | asset paths start with `/` | ✓ 0 relative `src`/`href` in `body.html`; 17 `/img/` + 14 `/fig/`. `/fonts/` is referenced from the `@font-face` in `app.css`, `/models/` and `/js/three/draco/` from `three3d.js` — all absolute. |
| 13 | `npm run build` | ✓ client + server, no SSR errors |
| 14 | looks identical in the browser | **unverified — needs a human look** |

### On item 9

Rendering the markup client-only was not the cause and would make things
slightly worse: it adds a frame where the page is genuinely empty, and it
delays the DOM that `app.js` needs. Server-rendering it is also safe — React
does not diff the children of a `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` node during
hydration, so no mismatch is possible there. `suppressHydrationWarning` is
still correct and now set, because `app.js` rewrites that subtree
immediately after mount.

## Still unverified

No headless browser is installed in this project, so the chain fix was
verified by reading the code and confirming every script serves HTTP 200,
not by observing the page render. The browser check is still outstanding,
and the Draco/CSP item below remains open.

