## FIX 5 — mobile excess spacing · FIXED (probable cause)

Not a `mobile.css` value — a wrapper bug. `prototype/js/app.js` ends with:

```js
document.fonts.ready.then(() => { fitTexts(); … ScrollTrigger.refresh() });
addEventListener('load', () => ScrollTrigger.refresh());
```

In the prototype those scripts run during initial parse, so the `load`
listener is registered before the event. Loaded from a React effect they
run much later and `window.load` has usually already fired, so that
listener never runs. Every pinned ScrollTrigger then keeps the start/end it
measured at `create()` time — before images and fonts settled — which shows
up as pins engaging at the wrong offset and stretches of empty space, worst
on mobile where `.m-sec` heights depend most on reflow.

`PrototypePage` now replays the missed hook after the chain completes:

```js
function replayMissedLifecycleHooks() {
  const refresh = () => window.ScrollTrigger?.refresh();
  if (document.readyState === 'complete') refresh();
  else window.addEventListener('load', refresh, {once: true});
  document.fonts?.ready?.then(refresh);
}
```

Flagged as *probable*: it is a real defect with a clear mechanism, but
whether it accounts for all of the reported space needs a browser check.
If space remains, the section name or a screenshot would pin it down.

