# CSP opened for three.js + Draco (2026-11-04) — approved by the user

## The change

`app/entry.server.jsx`, backed up to
`_backup/entry.server.jsx.20261104-163757`:

```js
scriptSrc: ["'self'", "'wasm-unsafe-eval'", 'blob:'],
workerSrc: ["'self'", 'blob:'],
childSrc:  ["'self'", 'blob:'],
```

Why each is needed, traced to the code:

| Directive | Needed by |
|---|---|
| `worker-src blob:` | `DRACOLoader.js` builds its decode Worker with `URL.createObjectURL(new Blob([...]))`. `worker-src` otherwise falls back to `default-src`, which has no `blob:`. |
| `script-src 'wasm-unsafe-eval'` | `js/three/draco/draco_wasm_wrapper.js` instantiates `draco_decoder.wasm`. WebAssembly compilation is gated on this token. |
| `child-src blob:` | Legacy fallback for `worker-src` in older engines. |

Scope: `blob:` is same-origin by construction — it permits only blobs this
document itself created, not any external origin. `'wasm-unsafe-eval'`
permits WebAssembly compilation only; it does not re-enable `eval()`.

### Verified: Hydrogen still injects its nonce

Adding an explicit `scriptSrc` could have dropped the nonce that
Hydrogen's own inline scripts rely on. It does not — the emitted header is:

```
script-src 'self' 'wasm-unsafe-eval' blob: 'nonce-<per-request>'
worker-src 'self' blob:
child-src  'self' blob:
```

`'self'` and the nonce coexist (no `'strict-dynamic'`), so both the
dynamically appended `/js/*.js` scripts and Hydrogen's nonce'd inline
scripts are allowed.

## Import map

Added to the server-rendered `<head>` in `app/root.jsx`, carrying the
nonce (`script-src` has one, and `'self'` does not cover inline scripts):

```html
<script type="importmap" nonce="…">
{"imports":{"three":"/js/three/three.module.js","three/addons/":"/js/three/addons/"}}
</script>
```

It is in the document rather than injected at runtime because an import
map must precede any module load, and browsers other than Chrome accept
only one. Verified in the served HTML: byte offset 509, inside `<head>`,
against the first `type="module"` at byte 116110.

`tools/sync-prototype.mjs` also rewrites `three3d.js` and the six three
addons to relative specifiers, so the map is a safety net rather than
load-bearing — it keeps a bare `three` import working if a future
prototype update reintroduces one.

## Already in place before this request

Items 2-5 of the request were already done by `tools/sync-prototype.mjs`:

- `prototype/js/three/` -> `public/js/three/` (10 files incl. `draco/`)
- `setDecoderPath('/js/three/draco/')`
